###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# Training time per epoch on COLL: SchNet 8.9 min, DimeNet++ 10.4 min, the
# five-model ensemble 31.2 min, MVE 13.6 min (Table 3); on QM9 U0 the
# DimeNet++ changes reduce the time per epoch from 35.4 to 4.3 min
# (Table 1). Hardware is not stated; no inference timing is given.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Introduces DimeNet++ ('we start from the recently proposed DimeNet ... and propose the DimeNet++ model'); the registry treats DimeNet++ as a variant of the DimeNet method, so no derivation edge is recorded. Introduces COLL; its size and level of theory are entered in the data-set registry from this paper, and its origin-paper stub is removed.
# - COLL split sizes are not stated in this workshop paper; the code that ran the DFT calculations is not named.
# - The ensemble of DimeNet++ models (0.050 eV, 0.038 eV/A) and the uncertainty correlations of Table 3 are not encoded.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: datacite).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/gasteiger2020coll.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

